\par\par \b \uc2 Press Release: \uc2 WISeKey International Holding Ltd\uc2  Signs Merger Agreement to Redomicile to the British Virgin Islands\b0\par\par\uc2 1,722 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires German\par \uc2 RTDJGE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 WISeKey International Holding Ltd\uc2  Signs Merger Agreement to Redomicile to the British Virgin Islands\par \par \uc2 Zug, Switzerland, June 29, 2026 -- Ad-Hoc announcement pursuant to Art. 53 of SIX Listing Rules -- \uc2 WISeKey International Holding AG\uc2  ("\uc2 WISeKey\uc2 ") (SIX: WIHN; Nasdaq: WKEY) today announced that it has signed a merger agreement with WISeKey International Corp., a British Virgin Islands company and wholly owned subsidiary of \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  ("WISeKey BVI"), to effect \uc2 WISeKey\uc2 's proposed redomiciliation from Switzerland to the British Virgin Islands.\par \par \uc2 Under the proposed transaction, \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  would merge with and into WISeKey BVI, with WISeKey BVI surviving the merger as the publicly traded parent company of the \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  group and successor to \uc2 WISeKey\uc2 . Following completion of the redomiciliation, WISeKey BVI is expected to have its ordinary shares directly listed both on Nasdaq, and on \uc2 SIX Swiss Exchange\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As part of the merger, each outstanding class of \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  shares will be exchanged for the relevant class of WISeKey BVI shares in accordance with the exchange ratios set out in the merger agreement. \uc2 WISeKey\uc2 's current American Depositary Share ("ADS") program will be terminated, and holders of \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  ADSs will receive WISeKey BVI ordinary shares in exchange.\par \par \uc2 The current holders of \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  Class B shares, being \uc2 WISeKey\uc2 's shares traded on the \uc2 SIX Swiss Exchange\uc2 , will have certain election rights among different classes of shares that differ with respect to voting rights and dividend rights. In the absence of an election by holders of \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  Class B shares, such holders will receive WISeKey BVI ordinary shares in exchange for their \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  Class B Shares. Detailed procedures for the share and ADS exchanges, including the available elections by shareholders and relevant deadlines, will be communicated separately in advance of the extraordinary general meeting of shareholders (the "EGM") at which \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  shareholders' approval for the redomiciliation will be sought. We currently expect the EGM to be held in the course of Q3 2026. No later than 30 days prior to the EGM, \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  shareholders will receive access to copies of the merger agreement, the merger report, and the audit report thereon, as well as \uc2 WISeKey\uc2 's standalone and consolidated annual financial statements and annual reports for the financial years 2025, 2024 and 2023, and the standalone financial statements of WISeKey BVI as of and for the period ended December 31, 2025.\par \par \uc2 The merger is intended to align the group's holding company jurisdiction with its international capital markets profile. The British Virgin Island's contemporary and flexible corporate legal framework is expected to provide WISeKey BVI with greater strategic and operational flexibility, including in terms of access to equity capital markets in the U.S. and Switzerland, and in support of future strategic initiatives. There can be no assurance that the anticipated benefits of the redomiciliation will be realized.\par \par \uc2 The completion of the merger remains subject to various customary conditions. Apart from the approval of the merger by shareholders at an EGM, this will include, among other things, the effectiveness of the registration statement to be filed with the \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 , the required Nasdaq and SIX listing authorizations, the confirmation by the Swiss Takeover Board that \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  will be subject to the same opting-out from the mandatory takeover provisions as \uc2 WISeKey\uc2 , and the satisfaction of Swiss law, BVI law, regulatory and procedural conditions.\par \par \uc2 About \uc2 WISeKey\par \par \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  (NASDAQ: WKEY; \uc2 SIX Swiss Exchange\uc2 : WIHN) is a leading global cybersecurity company currently deploying large scale digital identity ecosystems for people and objects using Blockchain, AI and IoT respecting the Human as the Fulcrum of the Internet. \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  microprocessors secure the pervasive computing shaping today's Internet of Everything. WISeKey IoT has an install base of over 1.5 billion microchips in virtually all IoT sectors (connected cars, smart cities, drones, agricultural sensors, anti-counterfeiting, smart lighting, servers, computers, mobile phones, crypto tokens etc.). \uc2 WISeKey\uc2  is uniquely positioned to be at the edge of IoT as our semiconductors produce a huge amount of Big Data that, when analyzed with \b \highlight22\uc2 Artificial Intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AI), can help industrial applications to predict the failure of their equipment before it happens.\par \par \uc2 Our technology is Trusted by the OISTE/\uc2 WISeKey\uc2 's Swiss based cryptographic Root of Trust ("RoT") provides secure authentication and identification, in both physical and virtual environments, for the Internet of Things, Blockchain and \b \highlight22\uc2 Artificial Intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The WISeKey RoT serves as a common trust anchor to ensure the integrity of online transactions among objects and between objects and people. For more information, visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=xCJ2L1MePtDmV6pVWF1wv4Etqt2w7KtbXP9RXWqZfcOqOA0aAbdd_7MHW1Cz_vaqHIs2XQ03XRby-IbmhfsxTIods1jfVy0-WGzIJbDC48ZQO5y-rDuIkCntztp8EYlnPhb-mGvqG4F-thOsRyobDqHZ7p0Yi4Uu57rBhfa1fWXuF3zbHLCdC5YuMGtNKK-e_gakCanwGeJtcBnA8lA9MxlxTEC8FgfCLoqViPKwC7k"}}{\fldrslt