\par\par \b \uc2 *South Korean Government, Companies Unveil New Investment Plan for Chips, AI\b0\par\par\uc2 506 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 08:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 29 Jun 2026 02:19 ET *South Korean Industry Minister: Around KRW800T to Build Chipmaking Hub in Southwest Korea\par \par \uc2 29 Jun 2026 02:19 ET *South Korean Science Minister: Over KRW1000T to Be Invested in Building AI Data Centers by 2035\par \par \uc2 29 Jun 2026 02:21 ET *\uc2 Samsung\uc2  Chairman: New Chip Hub to Be Built in Gwangju, Southwest Korea\par \par \uc2 29 Jun 2026 02:23 ET *\uc2 SK Group\uc2  Chairman: \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  to Invest KRW1,100T to Expand Chip Production in Korea\par \par \uc2 29 Jun 2026 02:25 ET *South Korea's Investment Plan Announced During Briefing Chaired by President \uc2 Lee Jae Myung\par \par \uc2 29 Jun 2026 04:18 ET  South Korea Announces Massive New Chip, AI Investment Plan\par \par \uc2 By Kwanwoo Jun\par \par \uc2 South Korea's government has laid out plans for massive outlays in semiconductor industries and \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  infrastructure, with memory-chip leaders \uc2 Samsung Electronics\uc2  and \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  committing to substantial new investments.\par \par \uc2 More than 3 quadrillion won, equivalent to nearly $2 trillion, will be spent in the years to come in creating fresh chip and AI industry hubs in South Korea.\par \par \uc2 The country's industry minister said at a televised government briefing on Monday that he expects the government and companies to invest around 800 trillion won to build new chip-making hubs in southwest Korea, 81 trillion won to build chip-packaging facilities in central Korea and 30 trillion won to secure an early foothold in emerging chip markets over the next 15 years.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the nation's science minister said he expects more than 1 quadrillion won to be invested by both the government and companies in building AI data centers by 2035.\par \par \uc2 The briefing was chaired by President \uc2 Lee Jae Myung\uc2 , who has called for large-scale investment in South Korea's semiconductor and AI industries, including robotics and AI data centers, while pledging strong government support for relevant businesses.\par \par \uc2 SK Group\uc2  Chairman Chey Tae-won said mobile carrier \uc2 SK Telecom\uc2  plans to build 15 gigawatts of AI data center capacity in Korea.\par \par \uc2 Chey also said \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  supplier \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  plans to invest 1.100 quadrillion won to expand its chip production in Korea in the future, and of the total, 400 trillion won has been earmarked for investment in a new facility in southwest Korea.\par \par \uc2 Samsung\uc2  Chairman Lee Jae-yong said that he has picked Gwangju in southwest Korea as a strong candidate to host a new \uc2 Samsung\uc2  chip production hub. \uc2 Samsung Electronics\uc2  said in a separate statement that it and other AI-related \uc2 Samsung\uc2  affiliates are also expanding their investments across the country, worth 2.655 quadrillion won in total.\par \par \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  and \uc2 Samsung\uc2 --alongside \uc2 Micron Technology\uc2  of the U.S.--are the world's leading suppliers of high bandwidth memory chips, which are crucial parts of \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 's AI accelerators and other advanced memory products for AI applications.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kwanwoo Jun at kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 29, 2026 04:18 ET (08:18 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260629em6t000vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
