\par\par \b \uc2 Press Release: \uc2 Eco Wave Power\uc2  Announces Closing of $4.0 Million Strategic Financing Priced at a Premium to Market to Advance Global Project Deployment and AI-Driven Technology\b0\par\par\uc2 1,243 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 14:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 STOCKHOLM, June 29, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- \uc2 Eco Wave Power Global AB\uc2  (publ) (NASDAQ: WAVE) ("\uc2 Eco Wave Power\uc2 " or the "Company"), a leading innovator in onshore wave energy technology, today announced the successful closing on June 26, 2026 of its previously announced registered direct offering with a single strategic institutional investor. The financing strengthens the Company's balance sheet to support the advancement of its global project portfolio and further develop its strategy of positioning wave energy as the renewable energy layer for AI infrastructure and expanding the Company's AI capabilities, including digital twins and other AI-driven technologies designed to optimize the performance, monitoring and scalability of its wave energy technology.\par \par \uc2 The Offering consisted of 400,000 American Depositary Shares ("ADSs") at an offering price of $10.00 per ADS, representing a 10.7% premium to the previous Nasdaq closing price. Gross proceeds from the Offering were approximately $4.0 million, before deducting placement agent fees and offering expenses.\par \par \uc2 "The successful completion of this financing marks another important milestone for \uc2 Eco Wave Power\uc2  as we continue advancing our global project portfolio," said \uc2 Inna Braverman\uc2 , Founder and Chief Executive Officer of \uc2 Eco Wave Power\uc2 . "With projects progressing across multiple international markets and growing global demand for reliable renewable energy to support digital infrastructure and AI, we believe this financing further strengthens our ability to execute our strategy while creating long-term value for our shareholders."\par \par \uc2 In connection with the Offering, the investor received warrants to purchase up to 300,000 ADSs. The warrants have an exercise price of SEK 116.76 per ADS (which is equal to US$12.00 per ADS), representing a 32.9% premium to the previous Nasdaq closing price, are exercisable immediately, and expire on June 26, 2029.\par \par \uc2 Maxim Group LLC\uc2  acted as the sole placement agent for the Offering.\par \par \uc2 Eco Wave Power\uc2  intends to use the net proceeds from the Offering to advance projects across its international pipeline while further positioning wave energy as the renewable energy layer for AI infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 The Offering was made pursuant to an effective shelf registration statement on Form F-3, as amended (File No. 333-275728), previously filed with and subsequently declared effective by the \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  ("SEC") on December 6, 2023. A prospectus supplement, dated June 26, 2026, relating to the ADSs issued in the Offering was filed by the Company with the SEC. Copies of the prospectus supplement relating to the Offering, together with the accompanying prospectus, can be obtained at the SEC's website at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sec.gov"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.sec.gov}}}\uc2  or by contacting \uc2 Maxim Group LLC\uc2 , 300 Park Avenue, 16th Floor, New York, NY 10022, Attention: Syndicate Department, via email at syndicate@maximgrp.com or by telephone at (212) 895-3745.\par \par \uc2 This press release shall not constitute an offer to sell or the solicitation of an offer to buy these securities, nor shall there be any sale of these securities in any state or other jurisdiction in which such offer, solicitation or sale would be unlawful prior to the registration or qualification under the securities laws of any such state or other jurisdiction.\par \par \uc2 About \uc2 Eco Wave Power Global AB\uc2  (publ)\par \par \uc2 Eco Wave Power Global\uc2  (NASDAQ: WAVE) is a pioneering onshore wave energy company that converts ocean and sea waves into clean, reliable and cost-efficient electricity using its patented technology. By generating renewable power directly from existing coastal infrastructure such as breakwaters, jetties and piers, \uc2 Eco Wave Power\uc2  enables sustainable electricity production in close proximity to coastal cities, ports and energy-intensive infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 As global electricity demand continues to rise, driven in part by the rapid growth of \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2 , data centers and digital infrastructure, \uc2 Eco Wave Power\uc2  is positioning its technology as a scalable, nearshore renewable energy solution capable of supporting next-generation power needs.\par \par \uc2 With a mission to accelerate the global transition to renewable energy while supporting the next generation of digital and industrial infrastructure, \uc2 Eco Wave Power\uc2  developed and operates Israel's first grid-connected wave energy power station, recognized as a "Pioneering Technology" by the Israeli Ministry of Energy and co-funded by \uc2 EDF Power Solutions\uc2 . In the United States, the Company recently launched the first-ever onshore wave energy pilot station at the \uc2 Port of Los Angeles\uc2 , in collaboration with Shell Marine Renewable Energy.\par \par \uc2 Eco Wave Power\uc2  is advancing projects in Portugal, Taiwan and India, representing a project pipeline of 404.7 MW. The Company has received international recognition and support from organizations including the European Union Regional Development Fund, Innovate UK and the EU Horizon 2020 program, and was honored with the United Nations Global Climate Action Award.\par \par \uc2 Eco Wave Power's American Depositary Shares (ADSs) are traded on the Nasdaq Capital Market under the ticker symbol "WAVE."\par \par \uc2 For more information, please visit:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.ecowavepower.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.ecowavepower.com}}}\par \par \uc2 For more information, please contact the Company's CFO:\par \par \uc2 Aharon Yehuda\par \par \uc2 Aharon@ecowavepower.com\par \par \uc2 +972 3 509 4017\par \par \uc2 Forward Looking Statements\par \par \uc2 This press release contains forward-looking statements within the meaning of the "safe harbor" provisions of the U.S. Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995 and other Federal securities laws. Forward-looking statements can be identified by words such as: "anticipate," "intend," "plan," "goal," "seek," "believe," "project," "estimate," "expect," "strategy," "future," "likely," "may," "should," "will", or variations of such words, and similar references to future periods. For example, the Company is using forward-looking statements in this press release when it discusses the intended use of proceeds from the Offering. These forward-looking statements and their implications are neither historical facts nor assurances of future performance and are based on the current expectations of the management of Eco Wave Power and are subject to a number of factors, uncertainties and changes in circumstances that are difficult to predict and may be outside of Eco Wave Power's control that could cause actual results to differ materially from those described in the forward-looking statements. Therefore, you should not rely on any of these forward-looking statements. Except as otherwise required by law, Eco Wave Power undertakes no obligation to publicly release any revisions to these forward-looking statements to reflect events or circumstances after the date hereof or to reflect the occurrence of unanticipated events. More detailed information about the risks and uncertainties affecting Eco Wave Power is contained under the heading "Risk Factors" in Eco Wave Power's Annual Report on Form 20-F for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2025 filed with the SEC on March 12, 2026, which is available on the SEC's website, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sec.gov"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.sec.gov}}}\uc2 , and other documents filed or furnished to the SEC. Any forward-looking statement made in this press release speaks only as of the date hereof. References and links to websites have been provided as a convenience and the information contained on such websites is not incorporated by reference into this press release.\par \par \uc2 Logo: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mma.prnewswire.com/media/2993116/Eco_Wave_Power_Logo.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://mma.prnewswire.com/media/2993116/Eco_Wave_Power_Logo.jpg}}}\par \par \uc2 View original content to download multimedia:{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/eco-wave-power-announces-closing-of-4-0-million-strategic-financing-priced-at-a-premium-to-market-to-advance-global-project-deployment-and-ai-driven-technology-302813118.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/eco-wave-power-announces-closing-of-4-0-million-strategic-financing-priced-at-a-premium-to-market-to-advance-global-project-deployment-and-ai-driven-technology-302813118.html}}}\par \par \uc2 SOURCE Eco Wave Power Global AB (publ)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 29, 2026 08:00 ET (12:00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260629em6t001n1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
