\par\par \b \uc2 EQS-News: \uc2 NFON\uc2  \u160\'00\'A0recognised for innovation and AI transformation:\u160\'00\'A0\uc2 NFON\uc2  named one of Germany\u8217\'20\'19s most innovative medium-sized companies\b0\par\par\uc2 1,479 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 14:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires German\par \uc2 RTDJGE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EQS-News: \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  / Key word(s): Miscellaneous \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  \u160\'00\'A0recognised for innovation and AI transformation:\u160\'00\'A0\f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  named one of Germany's most innovative medium-sized \par companies \par 2026-06-29 / 14:51 CET/CEST \par The issuer is solely responsible for the content of this announcement. \par  \par =---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  \u160\'00\'A0recognised for innovation and AI transformation:\u160\'00\'A0\f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  named one of Germany's most innovative medium-sized \par companies \par Munich, 29 June 2026 - \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a leading European provider of integrated business communications with a focus on \par AI-based applications, has been honoured with the TOP 100 Award 2026 as one of Germany's most innovative medium-sized \par companies. The independent scientific assessment recognises the achievements of \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  in transforming business \par communications through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It also confirms that \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  has established an innovation management \par system that sets international benchmarks.* \f28 \uc2 \f2 Andreas Wesselmann\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Chief Executive Officer of \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Jana Richter, \par Executive Vice President Engineering, AI & Innovation, accepted the award from former German President Christian Wulff \par at the German Mittelstand Summit in Heidelberg. \par While business communications were once primarily centred on accessibility and voice transmission, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial \par intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is fundamentally transforming the way organisations communicate, use knowledge and interact with their \par customers. They are evolving from a simple communication channel into an intelligent interface connecting people, \par information and business processes. This transformation is increasingly disrupting established market structures. \par AI at the heart of the \u160\'00\'A0innovation strategy \par With its NFON Next 2027 strategy, \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  has established a clear roadmap for setting priorities, focusing resources and \par translating innovation into scalable business models. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forms the cornerstone of the company's \par innovation and growth strategy and is consequently central to \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2 's ongoing strategic development. The objective is to \par establish \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  as Europe's leading provider and trusted partner for AI-based business communications. \par A decisive milestone on this journey was the acquisition of conversational AI specialist botario. This laid the \par foundations for building the company's own AI capabilities and accelerated \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2 's transformation from a cloud telephony \par provider into a business that places \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  firmly at the centre of its product and technology \par development. Its early investment in AI technologies now enables \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  to bring innovations to market more rapidly and \par set new standards in intelligent business communications. \par AI creates value for everyone\u160\'00\'A0 \u160\'00\'A0 \par For \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is not an end in itself. The aim is to help organisations make communications more \par productive, automate business processes more extensively and unlock new value creation potentials across the full \par spectrum of customer communications. The use of AI creates added value for customers while simultaneously strengthening \par the company's own performance through higher productivity, greater scalability and additional growth opportunities. \par The results of this development are now evident in \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2 's AI-based product portfolio. Built on a proprietary AI \par communications platform, proprietary AI speech-processing models and intelligent communication automation solutions, \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  has translated its AI strategy into practical products such as AI Essentials, Nia and Nia FrontDesk, integrating \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly into its customers' communication and service processes. By combining cloud telephony, \par conversational AI and intelligent assistant capabilities, \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  enables organisations to make better use of information, \par improve process efficiency and enhance customer interactions throughout the entire customer journey. In doing so, \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par is among the innovation leaders redefining the boundaries of traditional business communications. \par European values as a driver of innovation and competitive advantage \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2  is a European provider by conviction and by design. Its cloud infrastructure, commitment to data sovereignty and \par consistent focus on market requirements create trust and reliability in an environment where security, regulatory \par stability and digital sovereignty are becoming increasingly important. These factors strengthen \f28 \uc2 \f2 NFON\f28 \uc2 \f2 's competitive \par position and provide the foundation for sustainable innovation. The company's ambition is to identify technological \par developments at an early stage, translate them into market-relevant solutions and help shape the future of business \par communications as a European pioneer. \par "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is changing the rules of the game. The next generation of our market is emerging wherever \par communication, automation and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  work seamlessly together. Innovation does not come from waiting, \par but from having the courage to explore new paths. For us, this transformation means setting new standards for \par intelligent and trustworthy business communications," noted Andreas Wesselmann. "The TOP 100 Award confirms that we are \par on the right course and, above all, recognises the achievements of the people at NFON, whose enthusiasm for innovation, \par courage and creativity enable them to deliver measurable value for our customers every day." \par *The assessment confirms an exceptionally strong management commitment to innovation, supported by a clearly defined \par and consistently implemented innovation strategy in which digitalisation, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and cybersecurity are \par firmly embedded. Particularly noteworthy is the fact that NFON ranks among the top ten highest-rated companies in all \par four innovation management capability categories: innovation-oriented top management, innovation culture, innovative \par processes and organisation, and external orientation and open innovation. \par The assessment also confirms that NFON has highly professional innovation processes, including systematic monitoring of \par technology, markets and competitors, clear decision-making structures, a high degree of organisational flexibility, \par strong cross-functional collaboration and extensive use of modern technologies, including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \par innovation management of NFON AG was awarded the highest possible rating of A+, placing it above the average of the \par companies recognised. \par With the TOP 100 seal for 2026, NFON AG ranks among Germany's most innovative medium-sized companies. The competition \par is led academically by \par Professor Dr Nikolaus Franke of the Vienna University of Economics and Business. \par Further information:\u160\'00\'A0ttps://\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.top100.de/nfon-ag-2026/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.top100.de/nfon-ag-2026/}}}\uc2 \f2  \par Investor Relations contact\u160\'00\'A0 \par NFON AG \par Friederike Thyssen \par Vice President Corporate Affairs & Investor Relations \par +49 89 45300-449 \par ir-info@nfon.com \par Media contact \par NFON AG \par Thorsten Wehner \par Vice President Public Relations \par +49 89 45300-121 \par thorsten.wehner@nfon.com \par About NFON AG \par NFON AG is Europe's trusted partner for AI-based business communications. Founded in 2007 and headquartered in Munich, \par NFON enables companies to transform their communications using secure, scalable and AI-based technologies. \par Its integrated portfolio combines solutions in Business Telephony, Intelligent Assistant and Customer Engagement to \par help companies manage conversations, automate workflows and enhance the customer experience. By integrating AI into \par core communication processes, NFON enables smarter, data-driven interactions for organisations of all sizes. \par With its own subsidiaries in key European markets - including Germany, Austria, the United Kingdom, Italy, Spain, \par France, Poland, Portugal and Kosovo - NFON develops and operates its solutions in Europe, ensuring the highest \par standards of data protection, security and full GDPR compliance. \par Driven by its mission to rethink business communications and to inspire and connect people to grow sustainably \par together, NFON is shaping the future of secure, intelligent business communications "made in Europe". \par Further information can be found at\u160\'00\'A0\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://corporate.nfon.com/en/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://corporate.nfon.com/en/}}}\uc2 \f2 . \par For Germany:\u160\'00\'A0\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://corporate.nfon.com/de/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://corporate.nfon.com/de/}}}\uc2 \f2 . \par Disclaimer\u160\'00\'A0 \par This notification is provided for information purposes only and constitutes neither an offer to sell nor an invitation \par to buy or subscribe for the company's securities. The securities discussed in this notification are not and will not be \par registered under the US Securities Act of 1933 as amended ("US Securities Act") and are only permitted to be sold or \par offered for purchase in the United States of America after prior registration or on the basis of an exemption under the \par US Securities Act. No public offer of the securities discussed in this notification will be made in the United States \par of America and the information contained in this notification does not constitute an offer to buy securities. This \par notification is not intended for direct or indirect distribution, publication or dissemination to or within the United \par States of America, Australia, Canada, Japan or other countries in which the distribution of this notification is \par unlawful, or to US persons. \par  \par =---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \par 2026-06-29 CET/CEST Dissemination of a Corporate News, transmitted by EQS News - a service of EQS Group. \par The issuer is solely responsib