\par\par \b \uc2 Palantir\uc2  Stock Is Rising Again and This \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  Partnership Could Help the Recovery -- Barrons.com\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kit Norton \par \uc2 460 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 14:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Palantir Technologies\uc2  rose Monday as the stock continues to recover after snapping a seven-day losing streak on Friday. A new partnership with \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  could keep the stock moving higher after the recent selloff.\par \par \uc2 Palantir\uc2  stock advanced 4.2% to $117.65 in premarket trading on Monday and was set to add to a 5.3% gain from Friday.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Alex Karp\uc2 's software company have been in a rut in June, falling 25% and angling toward their worst monthly performance in five years. However, the stock ended a seven-day losing streak on Friday and could continue to advance on the strength of a newly announced partnership with \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Palantir\uc2  said Monday in a media release it has entered into a new strategic initiative with the chips giant to use the \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  AI ecosystem and Nvidia Nemotron -- \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  models -- to build custom models for the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Under the partnership, \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 's AI platform and \uc2 Palantir\uc2 's critical infrastructure products will come together to provide \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  agencies with a secure "intelligent engine" for training and the deployment of AI models.\par \par \uc2 "Combining \uc2 Palantir\uc2  infrastructure with \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 's AI and Nemotron models will allow the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  to unleash the full power of LLMs while removing the underlying security risks and rational concerns around proprietary insights migrating into the weights of closed models," \uc2 Palantir\uc2  CEO Karp said.\par \par \uc2 This isn't the first time \uc2 Palantir\uc2  has teamed up with \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  but the announcement comes at a fortuitous time for \uc2 Palantir\uc2  investors.\par \par \uc2 After three consecutive years of mammoth gains, \uc2 Palantir\uc2  stock has fallen 34% in 2026 on broad fears that AI could disrupt software. The pain for \uc2 Palantir\uc2  investors has ratcheted up in June, with shares sinking 25% on the back of that seven-day losing streak.\par \par \uc2 During the losing streak, spanning from June 16 to June 25, \uc2 Palantir\uc2  broke below multiple key levels of technical support. Shares have also traded well below their 50-day moving average as well as their 200-day moving average. \uc2 Palantir\uc2  stock's 50-day moving average currently around $136; the 200-day moving average is about $159, according to chart analysis.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Palantir\uc2  stock may have found its bottom after closing on Thursday at $107.27. The new \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  partnership might just be the catalyst to propel shares higher.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kit Norton at kit.norton@barrons.com\par \par \uc2 This content was created by Barron's, which is operated by Dow Jones & Co. Barron's is published independently from Dow Jones Newswires and The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 29, 2026 08:49 ET (12:49 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260629em6t0020r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
