\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Top Company Headlines at 9 AM ET: \uc2 Apple\uc2  Raises Prices on Macs, iPads by $200 or More on Some Models | \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  ...\b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 15:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2  Raises Prices on Macs, iPads by $200 or More on Some Models\par \par \uc2 The increases come a week after \uc2 Tim Cook\uc2  said higher memory costs made them "unavoidable."\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  Shakes Up Dimon Succession Race With Two New Presidents\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2  named \uc2 Doug Petno\uc2  and \uc2 Troy Rohrbaugh\uc2  as co-presidents of the company, laying the groundwork to find candidates to succeed chief executive \uc2 Jamie Dimon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Germany's Merck to Buy \uc2 Bio-Techne\uc2  for $11 Billion\par \par \uc2 Merck KGaA\uc2  offered $73 a share in cash for \uc2 Bio-Techne\uc2 , representing a 24% premium to the U.S. lab-tools supplier's closing price Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Darden\uc2  Posts Higher Sales but Warns of Slower Growth\par \par \uc2 Darden\uc2  posted higher profit and sales in its fiscal fourth quarter, once again led by its LongHorn Steakhouse brand, but expects growth to slow over the coming year.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2  Sees New AI Opportunities\par \par \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2  lifted its fiscal 2027 outlook on higher first-quarter results, driven by embedded-software growth and expanding opportunities with \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Winnebago\uc2  Cuts Outlook Amid Declining Sales\par \par \uc2 The motorhome maker posted a fiscal third-quarter profit of $14.5 million, or 51 cents a share, compared with $17.6 million, or 62 cents a share, in the same quarter a year ago.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 McCormick\uc2  Posts Higher Sales Amid Combination With \uc2 Unilever\par \par \uc2 The maker of spices and seasonings reported higher sales in its fiscal second quarter, as it continues work to combine with \uc2 Unilever\uc2 's food business.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  Claims Alibaba Ran 'Brazen' Campaign to Access Its \uc2 Claude AI\uc2  Model\par \par \uc2 U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  lab \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  has accused Chinese e-commerce giant \uc2 Alibaba\uc2  of "illicitly" accessing its frontier model Claude to harvest its capabilities.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  to Sell Majority Stake in Everllence For $8.4 Billion\par \par \uc2 Bain Capital\uc2  will buy 51% of heavy-engine business Everllence for $8.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 IBM\uc2  Stock Surges After Research Division Unveils a Sub-1-Nanometer Chip Prototype\par \par \uc2 IBM\uc2  debuts the first sub-1 nanometer chip, marking a step forward in the race to make AI chips smaller and more efficient.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to Invest Additional $13 Billion in India by 2030\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's planned spending to expand and support AI and cloud infrastructure in India builds on the $35 billion investment that was outlined last year.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 H&M\uc2  Hit by One-Off Costs as Turnaround Efforts Continue\par \par \uc2 Earnings were dented by $127.2 million in restructuring costs as the retailer made organizational changes.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Lockheed Martin\uc2  Lands $35 Billion Missile-Defense Deal\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon's order of Thaad interceptors follows the company's pledge to expand production over seven years.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Pizza Has Gone Cold. Domino's Is Still Worth a Look.\par \par \uc2 The category's sales are stagnant and its chains are faltering, but Domino's can emerge as a winner\par \par \uc2 -